        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first to play all cards from your hand onto the table.',
          gameplay: 'On your turn, you must either: 1. Play at least one card from your hand into a valid meld (new or existing). 2. Draw one card from the stock and end your turn.',
          keyRules: [
            'Must play at least one new card from hand each turn you play',
            'All table cards must form valid melds at end of turn',
            'Can manipulate any existing melds on the table',
            'Draw one card if unable or unwilling to play',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Don't 'dump' your easiest cards early. If you see a way to play a 7 of Hearts, wait until you have another card that depends on it. The more cards you put on the table, the more options your OPPONENTS have on their turns.",
          intermediate: "The Big Reveal: Wait until you can play 4-5 cards at once by rearranging the whole board. This 'explodes' your hand and often ends the game before opponents can react to the new board state.",
          advanced: "Defensive Manipulation: If you see an opponent looking for a 5 of Spades to finish their sequence, and that 5 is already in a 'Set of 5s' on the table, try to move that 5 into a DIFFERENT sequence that is harder for them to access.",
          tips: [
            "Sequences are better for manipulation than Sets. A sequence of 3-4-5-6 can be split into two 3-card melds if you have the right cards; a 3-card Set is 'atomic' and cannot be split.",
            "Always scan for 'orphan' cards. If you see a sequence of 4 cards, you can potentially take one end and use it elsewhere.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
